---
import LegalPage from "../../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Slot Recovery Terms of Use | Brad Traversy";
const description =
	"Terms of use for Slot Recovery, a Wix app by TravxLabs that helps businesses fill canceled appointment slots.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
	<LegalPage
		title="Terms of Use"
		intro="These terms govern a business's installation and use of Slot Recovery with Wix Bookings. By installing or using the app, you agree to these terms."
		updated="August 5, 2026"
	>
		<section>
			<h2>1. Provider and agreement</h2>
			<p>
				Slot Recovery is provided by <strong>TravxLabs</strong>, located at 7 Point
				Shore Road, Amesbury, Massachusetts 01913, United States. These Terms of Use
				form an agreement between TravxLabs and the person or business that installs
				or uses Slot Recovery. If you use the app for a business, you confirm that
				you have authority to accept these terms for that business.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>2. What Slot Recovery does</h2>
			<p>
				Slot Recovery helps Wix Bookings site owners maintain a consent-based list of
				clients interested in earlier appointments. When an appointment is canceled,
				the app can rank eligible clients, create a private response link, record a
				client's response, recheck availability, and let the site owner confirm a
				booking.
			</p>
			<p>
				The app does not guarantee that a cancellation will occur, that a client will
				accept an opening, or that a particular slot will remain available.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>3. Wix account and required products</h2>
			<p>
				You need an active Wix account, an eligible Wix site, and Wix Bookings to use
				Slot Recovery. You are responsible for your Wix account, site configuration,
				staff permissions, booking settings, and compliance with Wix terms. Features
				may be unavailable if Wix changes or disables a service the app depends on.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>4. Your responsibilities</h2>
			<p>You are responsible for:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Providing accurate service, staff, location, and availability information.</li>
				<li>Using the app only for lawful business purposes.</li>
				<li>Obtaining any consent required to contact clients.</li>
				<li>Reviewing each match and booking before confirming it.</li>
				<li>Honoring your own cancellation, refund, payment, and privacy policies.</li>
				<li>Responding to client questions and requests about their information.</li>
				<li>Protecting private response links from unauthorized access or distribution.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>5. Client consent and communications</h2>
			<p>
				A client joining a recovery list does not create or reserve an appointment.
				Slot Recovery records the consent submitted through the recovery form, but you
				remain responsible for determining whether and how you may contact that client.
				You must not send unsolicited, deceptive, unlawful, or abusive communications.
			</p>
			<p>
				Slot Recovery does not automatically send email or text messages. The site
				owner decides whether to contact a matched client and sends the private
				response link using its own communication method.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>6. Bookings and payments</h2>
			<p>
				A client's acceptance records interest in the offered opening but does not by
				itself create a booking. A booking is created only after the site owner
				separately confirms the action and the app verifies that the slot is still
				available.
			</p>
			<p>
				Slot Recovery does not collect or process payment. Any price, payment,
				cancellation, refund, tax, or dispute is handled through the site owner's Wix
				setup and policies.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
			<p>You may not use Slot Recovery to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Violate a law, regulation, court order, or third-party right.</li>
				<li>Collect information that is unnecessary for appointment recovery.</li>
				<li>Send spam or contact a person without the required consent.</li>
				<li>Attempt to bypass app permissions, authentication, or response-link controls.</li>
				<li>Interfere with the app, Wix, another site, or another user's data.</li>
				<li>Reverse engineer or exploit the service except where law expressly permits it.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>8. Sensitive and emergency use</h2>
			<p>
				Slot Recovery is an appointment workflow tool. It is not an emergency,
				medical-record, clinical decision, or crisis-communication system. Do not use
				it for urgent or life-critical communications. You are responsible for
				determining whether the app is appropriate for your industry and for avoiding
				information that your laws or professional obligations prohibit you from
				processing through the app.
			</p>
		</section>

